{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>ואשמע</b> — the reason is that they would swear by Him who lives, as in: \"Once I have sworn by My holiness\" (Psalms 89:35) — that is the Temple and that is the heavens, as in: \"For I lift up My hand to heaven\" (Deuteronomy 32:40), which I have already explained. For the eternal King, the Living One of the worlds, is HaShem, who gives life to all. And the meaning: He who causes them to stand, like giving life to man, and likewise: \"And You give life to them all\" (Nehemiah 9:6)."], :book :daniel, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {0 "The commentary concerns the oath formula in Daniel 12:7; the lemma ואשמע appears to be a truncated or variant citation of the verse's ואשמעה ('and I heard'), retained as-is."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Daniel - Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/daniel"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:21:30.452007739Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}